.TH DICTATE 1 "" "dictate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dictate \- dictation into the focused input on GNOME on Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dictate
.RI [ LANG | status | cancel ]
.br
.B dictate log
.RI [ N ]
.br
.B dictate setup
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The first press records, the second transcribes and inserts the text into the
input that had focus at the first. Bound to one shortcut per language by
.BR "dictate setup" ,
which also sets the input source and writes
.IR ~/.config/dictate/config .
While recording, the audio is transcribed at each pause and, with the ime
method, shown in the input, underlined; the text typed is the whole recording,
transcribed at the second press.
Run
.B dictate setup \-\-help
for its options.
.PP
Transcription is local by default. With DICTATE_BACKEND="openai" the audio is
sent to the OpenAI-compatible service at DICTATE_URL, and DICTATE_FALLBACK_URL
names a local whisper server for when that service fails or is slow.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dictate/config
The machine's defaults, written by the admin; the package ships none.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dictate/config
The user's settings, written by
.BR "dictate setup" ,
over the machine's. Both are KEY="value" lines, and a DICTATE_ variable in the
environment wins over both.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dictate/state
The current phase, read by the tray icon and
.BR dictate-status (1).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dictate/log
Every dictated text, when DICTATE_LOG="true": time, language, outcome and
text, one per line, readable by the user alone.
.B dictate log
prints the last
.I N
entries, 20 by default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dictate-status (1),
.BR dictate-indicator (1)
